## 4 Conclusions
In summary, we have employed P3HT-MWCNT composite as the high-performance HTL to fabricate carbon-based CsPbI2Br PSCs. The hydrophobic and dense P3HTMWCNT composite layer has a protective effect on the CsPbI2Br perovskite film by shielding it from the ambient moisture. The high charge carrier mobility of P3HTMWCNT composite enhances the holes extraction from perovskite film and decreases the recombination in the device. As a consequence, the carbon-based $\mathrm{Cs}\mathrm{Pb}{\mathrm{I}}_{2}\mathrm{Br}$ PSC with P3HT-MWCNT composite HTL achieves a champion conversion efficiency of $10.01\%$ which is much higher than those of the cells with P3HT HTL $(7.69\%)$ and without HTL $(5.52\%)$ . In addition, the carbon-based CsPbI2Br PSC with P3HTMWCNT composite HTL exhibits an excellent long-term stability under the ambient condition. This work here suggests a promising and practical strategy for improving the photovoltaic performance and long-term stability of inorganic PSCs.
